    "G10H2210/515": {
      "code": "G10H2210/515",
      "level": 9,
      "parent": "G10H2210/395",
      "ja": "バリ島音階，例．ガムランのためのもの，楽器はペアで演奏され，少し離してチューニングし全音栓ですべての音の対に一定の速度で干渉ビートが起こるようにする；バリ島のペンタトニック音階，例．バリ島のＳｌｅｎｄｒ？音階，または七音ペロッグ音階の５音モード，それ自体実質的に９音平均律の７音サブセット（５音ジャワ島ｓｌｅｎｄｒ？音階Ｇ１０Ｈ２２１０／５４１）",
      "en": "Balinese scales, e.g. for gamelan, with instruments played in pairs and tuned slightly apart to produce interference beating ideally at a consistent speed for all pairs of notes in all registers; Balinese pentatonic scales, e.g. Balinese slendro scale, or five-tone modes of the heptatonic pelog scale, itself substantially a 7-note subset of 9-tone equal temperament",
      "count": 2,
      "ipcCode": "CPCONLY",
      "coreCode": "G10H2210/515",
      "note": "",
      "sourceFile": "cpc_G10H.txt",
      "kind": "cpc"
    },
